# Page-by-page content outline (wireframe planning notes)

## Home

- Navigation bar (Home, About, Experience, Projects, Resume, Contact)
- Hero section
    - Name + “Java / Spring Developer” headline
    - 1–2 sentence value proposition
    - Primary CTA: View Resume
    - Secondary CTA: Contact
- About preview (3–5 lines + link)
- Experience preview (high-level bullets + link)
- Projects preview (2–3 featured project cards + link)
- Contact CTA strip (short line + button)
- Footer (GitHub, LinkedIn, email)

## About

- Short narrative: who I am + what I’m growing into
- Skills snapshot (Java, Spring Boot, APIs, SQL, Git, testing, etc.)
- What I’m learning now (optional)

## Experience

- Timeline or cards (role/project, dates, highlights)
- Emphasize impact + what I built

## Projects

- Featured projects (2–4)
- Each project includes:
    - Problem / goal
    - Tech stack
    - Key features
    - Screenshots (later)
    - Links: repo, live demo (later)

## Resume

- Embedded PDF view or download link
- One-click access from Home nav

## Contact

- Email + links (LinkedIn/GitHub)
- Optional contact form (name, email, message)
- Confirmation message after submit

---

# Mobile considerations

- Responsive navigation (hamburger menu)
- Readable typography (comfortable line length)
- Touch-friendly buttons (tap targets)
- Cards stack vertically; no tiny multi-column layouts
- Keep CTAs visible without excessive scrolling
